From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:37:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/37] [HW] Lower packed unions in HWAggregateToComb

!hw.union had no type conversion and no patterns; a struct holding a union
member reached comb.concat with a non-integer operand and asserted.

Convert unions to iN like structs and arrays; lower union_create to the
member's bits at its position (other bits zero; they are undefined) and
union_extract to a comb.extract of the member's range. The member's offset
counts from the MSB, matching how ExportVerilog pads a narrower member
(struct packed { pre_padding[offset]; member; post_padding }); a member as
wide as the union is the union itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
